                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "Area-X is the sequel to X-note, it contains most of the gameplay aspects and elements from the previous VN. \n\n[h1]Graphics[/h1]\nThe graphics in this VN is pretty much the same as the previous VN which I liked a lot. I was glad that the graphics stayed the same as I truly liked it the last time. \n[h1] Score: 10[/h1]\n\n[h1]Storyline[/h1]\nThis VN delivered such an amazing mystery story just like X-note. There are some puzzles to complete to progress in the story, but they aren't too hard to do. \n[h1]Score: 10[/h1]\n\n[h1]Sound[/h1]\nThe soundtrack definitely improved from the last game, which I was pleased about. The soundtracks seemed more appropriate in this VN and the soundtracks did not seem to repeat itself quite as often, but it still isn't top-notch soundtrack and there was no option for any kind of volume control in the \"Options\". \n[h1]Score: 7[/h1]\n\n[h1]Structure[/h1]\nThe artwork and the storyline make an awesome combination, the soundtrack was certainly improved, but I don't feel like it was enough. The \"Options\" menu barely had anything to change, there was no option to change the volume...it was either ON or OFF and there no other \"text\" options. Also, just like X-note, there is only 15 save slots which I feel isn't enough if someone is going to do all the 9 routes. \n[h1]Score: 8[/h1]\n\n[h1]Price[/h1]\nFor £18.99, this VN is over-priced just like the X-note. I would've liked to see the price reduced to at least £10 as it’s too expensive right now...\n[h1]Score: 5 [/h1]\n\nOverall Verdict: The VN has amazing artwork, a great story and a decent soundtrack going for it, but the lack of options in the \"options\" menu, save slots and the price might be the only aspects keeping this VN down.\n\nI totally recommend reading this VN if you have the money for it or you could just wait until it goes on sale.",
